※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4598

※ Taking a key out is writing, so it needs `mut` in the type.
※
※ A collection type written `mut ⸨K: V⸩` says what may be done to the table, and
※ taking a key out of it is one of those things: it is the same table everything
※ holding a handle to it reads, so one holding the read-only type cannot empty it
※ under the others.  `†` is refused there for the reason `d⸨k⸩ ← v` is (4598), and
※ reading `d⸨k⸩` is not: reading is what the read-only type is for.
※
※ Compare: **Rust**, where `remove` takes `&mut self` and the borrow checker says
※ the same thing; **C++**, where `erase` is not `const`; **Go**, which cannot say
※ it of a map at all.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let d: ⸨str: u64⸩ = ⸨"a": 1u64⸩
    ※ reading is allowed
    let held: u64 = d⸨"a"⸩ ?? 0u64
    ※ and taking out is not
    †d⸨"a"⸩
    if held = 1u64: 0u6 else: 1u6
